From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nuubOS: Square Pixels crop and bezel for any Picture Position

NUUBOS_RA_PIXEL_CROP=<n> (nuubos-emud, per-game Square Pixels aspect):
smart integer scaling takes the vertical factor even when the picture
is then at most n game pixels a side wider than the screen, cropped
evenly by patch 0003. With n = 8 a 256-wide SNES picture is 768x672 on
the 720x720 RG CubeXX (8 pixels cut a side) instead of a 720x630 fit.

The bezel of patch 0010 puts its strip (silhouette, logo, accent line)
in the larger of the bands above and below the picture, so a picture
centred or at the bottom (Picture Position, video_viewport_bias_y) keeps
its decoration; side panels only fill the rows beside the picture.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [nuubOS specific]
---
--- a/gfx/video_driver.c
+++ b/gfx/video_driver.c
@@ -2536,6 +2536,25 @@
    return keep;
 }
 
+/* nuubOS: NUUBOS_RA_PIXEL_CROP=<n> (set by nuubos-emud for the per-game
+ * Square Pixels aspect) lets smart integer scaling take the vertical
+ * factor even when the picture is then wider than the screen by at most
+ * n of the game's pixels a side, cropped evenly (patch 0003): a 256-wide
+ * SNES picture is 768x672 at 3x on the RG CubeXX's 720x720, 24 screen
+ * columns (8 game pixels) cut a side, instead of 2x or a 720x630 fit.
+ * Returns n, 0 = off. */
+static unsigned nuubos_pixel_crop(void)
+{
+   static int crop = -1;
+   if (crop < 0)
+   {
+      const char *s = getenv("NUUBOS_RA_PIXEL_CROP");
+      int n         = s ? atoi(s) : 0;
+      crop          = (n > 0 && n < 64) ? n : 0;
+   }
+   return (unsigned)crop;
+}
+
 /**
  * video_viewport_get_scaled_integer:
  * @vp            : Viewport handle
@@ -2698,6 +2717,10 @@
